* GIT — git for hash-file records, modelled on real git.  The "path" is an MVX
* file plus record id; the working tree is the live records.  GITIGNORE (an
* account record) keeps bulk data out of history; DICT addresses a dictionary.
*
* One source, two platforms, via $IFDEF MVX:
*   MVX — the engine (libmvxrt) reads records AND does the git objects, so the
*     verb is a thin CMD-framework dispatch to the GIT.* programs, each a one-line
*     CALL into the engine.
*   UniData — CallC gives C no file API, so the verb itself drives the record loop
*     natively (OPEN/SELECT/READNEXT/READ/WRITE) and calls C only for git objects
*     via CallC (Model B): no InterCall, no second session, no extra licence.
* The remote/clone/tag ops are MVX-only for now; on UniData they fall through to
* the usage line until the record-git engine's new subs are bridged into CallC.
$IFDEF MVX
* --- MVX: CMD-framework dispatch (the engine does the work) ------------------
* The command framework: git calls CMD.* directly.  A minimal copy is bundled in
* CMD.BP so git runs standalone; when the full mv_cmd is installed its catalog
* entry overrides the bundled one, so the same calls bind to whichever CMD.* is
* present — no probe, no rebuild.
CALL CMD.INIT("GIT", "version-control hash-file records")
CALL CMD.ADD("INIT", "create the record repository", "GIT.INIT")
CALL CMD.ADD("ADD", "stage records (file {id})", "GIT.ADD")
CALL CMD.ADD("RM", "unstage a record (file id)", "GIT.RM")
CALL CMD.ADD("IGNORE", "keep records out of history (pattern)", "GIT.IGNORE")
CALL CMD.ADD("STATUS", "show staged / changed records", "GIT.STATUS")
CALL CMD.ADD("COMMIT", "commit staged records (-m msg)", "GIT.COMMIT")
CALL CMD.ADD("LOG", "commit history", "GIT.LOG")
CALL CMD.ADD("DIFF", "unstaged record changes {file}", "GIT.DIFF")
CALL CMD.ADD("SHOW", "committed content of a record (file id)", "GIT.SHOW")
CALL CMD.ADD("RESTORE", "restore records from HEAD (file)", "GIT.RESTORE")
CALL CMD.ADD("BRANCH", "list or create a branch (name)", "GIT.BRANCH")
CALL CMD.ADD("CHECKOUT", "switch branch, update records (name)", "GIT.CHECKOUT")
CALL CMD.ADD("MERGE", "merge a branch into this one (name)", "GIT.MERGE")
CALL CMD.ADD("CHERRY-PICK", "apply one commit (commit)", "GIT.CHERRYPICK")
